## Destination Guide
Shimla (Hindi: शिमला), previously spelt Simla, is the capital of the state of Himachal Pradesh in India. It is a very popular holiday retreat during the summer months and is well known for its Victorian architecture, which is reflected in certain areas of the Mall and the Ridge. It is also a famous holiday spot for honeymoon.
## Best Time to Visit
- **Best Season:** October to November
- **Peak Tourist Season:** June, July-August
## Top Attractions & Activities
1. **Kufri** - Enjoy beautiful mountain views, forests, and outdoor activities. A short drive from most Shimla hotels will take you to Kufri, a small hill station known for its scenic beauty and adventure activities, like skiing and horse riding. ([Source](https://www.radissonhotels.com/en-us/blog/destination/things-to-do-in-shimla))
2. **Kalka–Shimla Toy Train** - Take a scenic train journey through tunnels, bridges, forests, and mountain landscapes. ([Source](https://www.facebook.com/realhimachal/videos/05-best-places-to-visit-in-shimlaplanning-a-trip-to-shimla-here-are-5-popular-pl/1411482477622547))
3. **Mall Road** - Walk around the heart of Shimla, explore shops, cafés, and enjoy the lively hill-station atmosphere. ([Source](https://www.facebook.com/realhimachal/videos/05-best-places-to-visit-in-shimlaplanning-a-trip-to-shimla-here-are-5-popular-pl/1411482477622547))
4. **Jakhu Temple** - Visit this famous temple located on Jakhu Hill and enjoy peaceful surroundings and mountain views. ([Source](https://www.facebook.com/realhimachal/videos/05-best-places-to-visit-in-shimlaplanning-a-trip-to-shimla-here-are-5-popular-pl/1411482477622547))
5. **The Ridge** - One of Shimla's most famous spots, offering open views of the mountains and easy access to the city's main attractions. ([Source](https://www.facebook.com/realhimachal/videos/05-best-places-to-visit-in-shimlaplanning-a-trip-to-shimla-here-are-5-popular-pl/1411482477622547))
6. **Viceregal Lodge & Botanical Gardens** - Explore the former Viceregal Lodge, now Indian Institute of Advanced Study, and the beautiful Botanical Gardens. ([Source](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tourist_attractions_in_Shimla))
7. **Shri Hanuman Mandir Jakhoo** - Experience authentic cultural flavors of Shimla at this famous temple located on Jakhu Hill. ([Source](https://www.makemytrip.com/tripideas/places/shimla))
8. **Christ Church** - Discover the colonial charm and history of Christ Church, a significant landmark in Shimla. ([Source](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tourist_attractions_in_Shimla))
9. **Indian Institute of Advanced Study** - Visit this prestigious institution known for its academic and cultural significance. ([Source](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tourist_attractions_in_Shimla))
10. **Scandal Point** - Explore Scandal Point, a scenic spot offering panoramic views of the city and surrounding hills. ([Source](https://www.makemytrip.com/tripideas/places/shimla))
## Local Food & Cuisine
1. **Kurkej** - A vegetarian dish made out of a variety of veggies like mashed potato, cauliflower, carrot etc. in the shape of a stick and deep fried. ([Source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pya0CXTvfjQ))
2. **Luchi Chole** - A popular dish consisting of luchi (deep-fried bread) served with chole (chickpeas curry). ([Source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pya0CXTvfjQ))
3. **Butter Chicken** - A classic Indian dish known for its rich and creamy gravy. ([Source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pya0CXTvfjQ))
4. **Chicken Curry** - Experience the flavors of a traditional chicken curry, often served with rice or bread. ([Source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pya0CXTvfjQ))
5. **Shimla Brewing Company** - Enjoy craft beers and cocktails at Shimla Brewing Company, a popular spot for both locals and tourists. ([Source](https://www.facebook.com/realhimachal/videos/6-best-dining-places-in-shimla-%EF%B8%8F%EF%B8%8F-food-ambience-youll-loveplanning-a-trip-to-shi/27966877916310493))
## Travel Tips
### Local Transportation
- **Public Transportation:** Local buses run from 7 a.m. to 9 p.m. Fares vary based on destination and can be bought once boarded. ([Source](https://www.kayak.com/Shimla.8835.guide))
- **Taxi:** Fare for a short ride is around ₹5-₹10, and up to ₹50 for longer rides. ([Source](https://www.kayak.com/Shimla.8835.guide))

### Safety & Cultural Etiquette
- **Travel Tips:** Modest clothing is appreciated, especially when visiting temples or rural communities. ([Source](https://www.rivieratravel.co.uk/blog/essential-travel-tips-visiting-india-health-safety-culture-more))

### Estimated Expenses (INR)
- **Budget Guide:** Approx. ₹1,500 – ₹2,500 per person per day includes budget accommodation, food, local transport, and sightseeing. ([Source](https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZTupYriWAs))
- **Food:** A typical meal in Shimla costs around ₹50-₹100, while a beer or cocktail can cost around ₹150. ([Source](https://www.trip.com/guide/info/trip-to-shimla-cost.html))
- **Transport:** Fare for a short ride is around ₹5-₹10, and up to ₹50 for longer rides. ([Source](https://www.kayak.com/Shimla.8835.guide))

### First-Time Visitor Advice
- **Travel Tips:** Walk the Mall Road, visit the colonial-era buildings, eat well, and let your body begin to adjust. ([Source](https://travelmelodies.com/india-travel-tips))
## Festivals & Events
- **Lavi Fair:** Held in Shimla district from November 11-14, this fair is the biggest commercial event and celebrates a trade treaty between the Bushahr kingdom and Tibet. ([Source](https://refuje.com/blog/himachal-pradesh-festivals-2026))